                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "55544372",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198184897393",
                            "num_reviews": 668,
                            "playtime_forever": 698,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 698,
                            "last_played": 1570736315
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Mixed. It is an interesting idea and concept, just not executed as well as I would prefer. Most of the day is idle and at full speed, with a few select times where I pause every other second to efficiently use teacher energy. Some of the scenarios seem to be designed with the intent of failing, which is maybe the way the developer wanted to drive the point of the game home. \n\nIn the end it gets tedious. This is better to be viewed as political art more so than a game, at that point I can understand the allure it may have. \n\n[h1]Additional Details[/h1]\n[table]\n   [tr]\n        [td]Operating System[/td]\n        [td]Ubuntu Linux 18.04 x64[/td]\n    [/tr]\n    [tr]\n        [td]CPU[/td]\n        [td]Ryzen 5 1500x[/td]\n    [/tr]\n    [tr]\n        [td]GPU[/td]\n        [td]GTX 1050, nvidia-410.78[/td]\n    [/tr]\n    [tr]\n        [td]Game Saves[/td]\n        [td]Seemingly automatically after each day, but there is not always confirmation[/td]\n    [/tr]\n    [tr]\n        [td]Notes[/td]\n        [td]Achievements trigger on exit; game speed seems to randomly adjust down sometimes[/td]\n    [/tr]\n    [tr]\n        [td]Technical Notes[/td]\n        [td]Unity game engine, no problems[/td]\n    [/tr]\n[/table]",
